# Performance Optimization Plan

The application is currently slow due to fetching all 140,000+ emission records for routine tasks like notification badges and full report displays. This plan introduces server-side pagination, specialized summary endpoints, and better indexing.

## Proposed Changes

### [Server-Side Optimizations]

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js)
- **New Endpoint**: `/api/emissions/summary` - Returns only the current year's total emissions and goal status for notifications.
- **Paginate Endpoint**: Update `/api/emissions` to support pagination (`?limit=100&offset=0`).
- **New Endpoint**: `/api/emissions/filters` - Returns unique years and other filter values without fetching full records.
- **Index Optimization**: Add `idx_emissions_status` and `idx_emissions_process_type` (if possible) or at least `idx_emissions_combined` for year/facility.
- **Refactor Summary Query**: Optimize the `LIKE` queries in `/api/dashboard/summary`.

### [Frontend Optimizations]

#### [MODIFY] [notification-logic.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/notification-logic.js)
- Switch from [fetch('/api/emissions')](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/carbon-intensity.js#194-225) to the new `/api/emissions/summary` endpoint.
- This will reduce the payload from ~50MB to a few bytes.

#### [MODIFY] [reports-logic.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/reports-logic.js)
- Implement server-side pagination.
- Use the new `/api/emissions/filters` endpoint to populate filter dropdowns.
- Avoid storing `rawData` with 140k items.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Monitor the `Network` tab in browser developer tools to verify payload size reductions.
- Measure API response times for the new endpoints compared to the old ones.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that the dashboard loads significantly faster.
- Verify that the notification badge still works correctly.
- Verify that pagination in reports works smoothly.
